{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789779179,"nonce":"3EDF9VLQvXmQuPdSkqFczYkC9Jg=","title":"LLVM tier declines functions passing or returning aggregates","message":"llvm_entry_abi_supported admits only scalar parameters and returns (plus\ngrowable list headers by pointer), so a function taking or returning a\nstruct is never promoted to LLVM and stays on Cranelift. Shaped tuples in\nthe Python frontend make every function that takes or returns a tuple such\na function.\n\nFix: give the LLVM entry the same convention Cranelift uses: an aggregate\nparameter arrives as the address of its bytes, a returned aggregate is\nwritten through a leading destination pointer that is also returned.","files":null}]}